---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="HistoAtlas · Terms of Service"
  description="Terms of service for HistoAtlas."
  canonicalUrl="/terms/"
>
  <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-12">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-3">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-zinc-500 mb-8">Last updated: February 2026</p>

    <div class="space-y-8 text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-2">Acceptance of Terms</h2>
        <p>
          By accessing or using HistoAtlas, you agree to be bound by these Terms of Service. If you
          do not agree to these terms, please do not use the service.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-2">Description of Service</h2>
        <p>
          HistoAtlas is an exploratory research tool for visualizing and analyzing morphological
          patterns in solid tumors derived from whole-slide histology images. It provides
          interactive embedding visualizations, cluster characterizations, and statistical
          association analyses. HistoAtlas is designed for research exploration and
          hypothesis generation. It is not a clinical or diagnostic tool.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-2">Data Sources &amp; Attribution</h2>
        <p>
          The data presented in HistoAtlas is derived from publicly available datasets, primarily:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside mt-2 space-y-1">
          <li>The Cancer Genome Atlas (TCGA) via the Genomic Data Commons (GDC)</li>
          <li>PanCancerAtlas integrated datasets</li>
          <li>Immune subtype classifications (Thorsson et al., <em>Immunity</em>, 2018)</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-2">
          No protected health information (PHI) is stored or served. TCGA sample identifiers are
          treated as research identifiers only and cannot be linked back to individual patients.
          All source data is subject to
          <a href="https://gdc.cancer.gov/about-gdc/gdc-policies" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GDC data use policies</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-2">Permitted Use</h2>
        <p>You may use HistoAtlas for:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside mt-2 space-y-1">
          <li>Educational purposes and learning about tumor morphology</li>
          <li>Academic and non-commercial research</li>
          <li>Hypothesis generation and exploratory data analysis</li>
          <li>Generating figures and exports for research publications (with appropriate citation)</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-2">You must not use HistoAtlas for:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside mt-2 space-y-1">
          <li>Clinical decision-making, patient diagnosis, or treatment planning</li>
          <li>Any purpose that would violate TCGA/GDC data use agreements</li>
          <li>Attempting to re-identify patients from research identifiers or derived data</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-2">Intellectual Property</h2>
        <p>
          Source data is made available under TCGA/GDC data use policies and the respective
          policies of contributing studies. Derived statistical analyses, visualizations, and
          precomputed results presented through HistoAtlas are provided as-is for research use.
          The HistoAtlas source code is available under the terms specified in our
          <a href="https://github.com/PABannier/tumor-morpho-map" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub repository</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-2">Disclaimers</h2>
        <p>
          HistoAtlas is not medical software and does not provide medical advice, diagnosis, or
          treatment recommendations. The statistical associations and visualizations presented are
          exploratory in nature and should not be interpreted as established clinical findings.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          The service is provided "as is" and "as available" without warranties of any kind,
          whether express or implied, including but not limited to warranties of merchantability,
          fitness for a particular purpose, accuracy, or non-infringement.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-2">Limitation of Liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, the maintainers and contributors of
          HistoAtlas shall not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or
          punitive damages, or any loss of data, profits, or goodwill, arising out of or in
          connection with your use of the service.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-2">Changes to These Terms</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these Terms of Service as the project evolves. Material changes will be
          reflected in the "Last updated" date above. Continued use of HistoAtlas after changes
          are posted constitutes acceptance of the revised terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-2">Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For questions or concerns about these terms, please open an issue on our
          <a href="https://github.com/PABannier/tumor-morpho-map" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub repository</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
